argSlotWriteT -- SEQ 420 R0 (2026-10-26): controls for the argument write-through cure, each a callee the jitter builds
ALONE (called from top level or by itself), so its own argument is the SEQ 380 argument slot.
SW-1 a self-recursive function that writes its argument (++argument) in every activation: the per-activation binding.
SW-2 / SW-3 a literal argument, lfF(4), written by the callee -- called twice, so a write that reaches the literal's node
shows on the second call.
SW-4 a computed argument, cfF(cfN - 1), written by the callee: cfN must not move.
Each row is read against the interpreted twin (`jitter;` -> `jitterOff;`).
